    "narrative": "The Sunday slate for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on two high-upside plays against Freddy Peralta, who remains a targetable arm despite his pedigree. **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91) and **Corbin Carroll** (73.48) represent our most potent options; **Tyler Soderstrom** leverages a significant park factor boost and an ideal #2 spot in the order, while **Corbin Carroll** remains the engine of our stolen base strategy, benefitting from a solid platoon advantage against Hughes. **Isaac Paredes** (63.56) also earns a Strong start, as a favorable wind forecast and a solid platoon split against the right-handed Blade Tidwell provide a clear path to high-value production despite the respectable xERA of the opposing starter.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical concerns today, most notably the rain risk hovering over **Austin Riley** (50.50). With a 37% probability of precipitation, **Austin Riley** sits in our \"marginal\" tier, and we will monitor the situation closely to avoid burning a game cap if a delay leads to a shortened appearance. While our bench is currently thinned by the injury status of **James Wood** and **Vinnie Pasquantino**\u2014both still sidelined\u2014and a scheduled off-day for **Josh Naylor**, our depth remains secure. **Gabriel Moreno** (57.18) and **Brice Turang** (57.64) are locked into the lineup based on high floor expectations; both narrowly held off internal challengers by virtue of their guaranteed spots in the upper third of their respective batting orders. Even with **Henry Bolte** (53.81) facing a tough test against Peralta, his park-adjusted metrics maintain his status as a viable starter to round out the outfield.",
